@page "/finance/cash-forecast"
@page "/finance"
@page "/finance/cash-summary"
@using Jewel.JPMS.Commercial
@using Jewel.JPMS.Features.Cashflow
@using static Jewel.JPMS.Features.Cashflow.CashflowDisplay
@using Jewel.JPMS.Contracts.Projects
@using Jewel.JPMS.Contracts.Retention
@using Jewel.JPMS.Features.Commercial
@using Jewel.JPMS.Features.Procurement
@using Jewel.JPMS.Features.Projects
@inject AuthService Auth
@inject SessionService Session
@inject ProjectListReadModel Projects
@inject ProjectFinancialSummaryReadModel Summary
@inject ProjectWorkOrdersReadModel WorkOrders
@inject ValuationLinesReadModel Lines
@inject ValuationClaimsReadModel Claims
@inject ClaimLinesReadModel ClaimEntries
@inject IValuationInvoiceStore Invoices
@inject IProjectContractStore Contracts
@inject IXeroCashSummaryStore Cash
@inject ForecastOverheadsStorage OverheadsStorage
@inject IQueryClient Queries
@inject ICommandSender Commands
@inject NavigationManager Nav
@implements IDisposable

<PageTitle>Cash Forecast · JPMS</PageTitle>

@*
    The company Cash Forecast (the sidebar's Financial Reports folder) — successor to the Cash
    Summary on the same slugs (/finance and /finance/cash-summary still land here; the canonical
    route is /finance/cash-forecast).

    Two sections, one load:

    FORECAST (top) — the time axis the Cash Summary never had: every known future cash movement
    placed in the month it is expected to land (CashForecastPhasing, contracts — pure and
    unit-tested), a net movement line, and for directors the running bank balance seeded from
    Xero, with the lowest point flagged. The phasing RULES are the interim set from
    docs/Financial-Reports-and-Nav-Refactor-Plan.md §4, awaiting FD/consultant sign-off — hence
    the standing amber notice. The figures being phased are the statements' own (RowFor below),
    so each project's months sum to its Project Completion Cashflow to the penny — checked live
    in the reconciliation footer, red if it ever fails.

    POSITION TO COMPLETION (below the divider) — the former Cash Summary, unchanged: the
    combined to-completion statement and the by-project table (finance meeting 2026-08-03,
    retired page Pages/CashSummary.razor). Kept while the forecast is unconfirmed so nothing
    anyone relies on disappears; the old bank tiles are not duplicated here — their figures live
    in the KPI strip on top.

    Figures come from exactly the same sources and arithmetic as each project's Cashflow tab
    (ValuationSummaryFigures, RetentionSchedule, ProjectDrawdown, part-payment-aware unpaid
    bills), so this page and the per-project statement can never disagree.

    The Future valuations row carries the FD's two per-project knobs (2026-08-13 — "France's
    next valuation won't be till next month… Woodhouse seems to be a lot less than that…
    Abbott will probably land up being more"), edited inline on its expanded lines: WHEN the
    next valuation lands (the project's NextExpectedValuationDate) and roughly how much the
    architect is expected to certify per month (ExpectedMonthlyValuation). With a monthly
    figure set, the engine claims at that rate until left-to-claim runs out instead of
    spreading evenly to practical completion — the AMOUNT is still the statement's, only its
    timing moves, so the tie-back below stays exact. Both are stored on the project (API-gated
    Director/FD/PM), so the tweak survives reloads and every colleague sees the same forecast.
*@

<ApprovedSessionGate>
    <section class="px-6 md:px-8 py-8 md:py-12">
        <header class="mb-4">
            <p class="eyebrow mb-1">JPMS · Company</p>
            <h1 class="text-2xl md:text-3xl font-semibold text-content leading-tight">Cash Forecast</h1>
            <p class="text-sm text-content-muted mt-1">
                Every known future cash movement in the month it is expected to land@(IsDirector ? ", and the bank balance that results — lowest point first" : "").
            </p>
        </header>

        @* Standing notice until the FD and consultant sign off the §4 phasing rules — the
           AMOUNTS are live and tie to the statements; only their TIMING is provisional. *@
        <p class="rounded-lg bg-amber-500/10 border border-amber-500/30 px-3 py-2 text-sm text-amber-600 mb-6 max-w-4xl">
            <span class="font-semibold">Unconfirmed figures.</span> The timing rules behind this
            forecast are awaiting sign-off (Financial-Reports-and-Nav-Refactor-Plan §4). Amounts
            are live and reconcile to the statement below; treat the months as indicative. Two
            known simplifications: supplier bills are assumed payable this month (per-bill due
            dates come with the confirmed build), and the overheads figure is entered on this
            page, not yet a system setting.
        </p>

        @{
            // Computed ONCE per render and threaded through — the KPI strip, the table, the
            // chart and the reconciliation check must all describe the same forecast.
            var forecastView = TableReady && SelectedProjects.Count > 0 ? BuildForecast() : null;
        }

        @* ── KPI strip, directors only — every tile is anchored to the bank position (mirrors
           the API's directors-only gate). Tiles keep their shape while loading: label stays,
           figure pulses. ── *@
        @if (IsDirector)
        {
            <div class="grid gap-4 sm:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-4 mb-8">
                <div class="rounded-xl border border-line bg-surface px-5 py-4">
                    <p class="text-[11px] uppercase tracking-wider text-content-subtle font-semibold mb-1">Cash in bank</p>
                    @if (BankSnapshot is null)
                    {
                        <p class="text-2xl font-semibold text-content flex items-center h-8" role="status" aria-live="polite" aria-busy="true">
                            <JewelIcon Class="w-4 h-4 animate-jewel-pulse" />
                            <span class="sr-only">Loading cash in bank</span>
                        </p>
                    }
                    else if (!BankSnapshot.IsConfigured || BankSnapshot.Error is not null)
                    {
                        <p class="text-sm text-content-muted mt-1">@(BankSnapshot.Error ?? "Xero isn't connected — add the Xero__ClientId / Xero__ClientSecret app settings.")</p>
                    }
                    else
                    {
                        <p class="text-2xl font-semibold text-content">@Money(BankSnapshot.TotalCash)</p>
                        <p class="text-xs text-content-subtle mt-1">@BankSnapshot.BankAccounts.Count @(BankSnapshot.BankAccounts.Count == 1 ? "account" : "accounts") · fetched @FetchedText</p>
                    }
                </div>
                <div class="rounded-xl border border-line bg-surface px-5 py-4"
                     title="The lowest the forecast bank balance gets across the visible months — the month to plan for.">
                    <p class="text-[11px] uppercase tracking-wider text-content-subtle font-semibold mb-1">Lowest forecast balance</p>
                    @if (!BankReady || !TableReady)
                    {
                        <p class="text-2xl font-semibold text-content flex items-center h-8" role="status" aria-live="polite" aria-busy="true">
                            <JewelIcon Class="w-4 h-4 animate-jewel-pulse" />
                            <span class="sr-only">Loading lowest forecast balance</span>
                        </p>
                    }
                    else if (forecastView is not { } low || low.Closing.Length == 0)
                    {
                        <p class="text-sm text-content-muted mt-1">Needs the bank position from Xero.</p>
                    }
                    else
                    {
                        <p class="text-2xl font-semibold @(low.Closing[low.MinIndex] < 0m ? "text-negative" : "text-content")">@Money(low.Closing[low.MinIndex])</p>
                        <p class="text-xs text-content-subtle mt-1">@MonthLabel(low.Axis[low.MinIndex]) — the month to plan for</p>
                    }
                </div>
                <div class="rounded-xl border border-line bg-surface px-5 py-4">
                    <p class="text-[11px] uppercase tracking-wider text-content-subtle font-semibold mb-1">Outstanding sales invoices</p>
                    @if (BankSnapshot is null)
                    {
                        <p class="text-2xl font-semibold text-content flex items-center h-8" role="status" aria-live="polite" aria-busy="true">
                            <JewelIcon Class="w-4 h-4 animate-jewel-pulse" />
                            <span class="sr-only">Loading outstanding sales invoices</span>
                        </p>
                    }
                    else if (!BankSnapshot.IsConfigured || BankSnapshot.Error is not null)
                    {
                        <p class="text-sm text-content-muted mt-1">—</p>
                    }
                    else
                    {
                        <p class="text-2xl font-semibold text-content">@Money(BankSnapshot.TotalOutstanding)</p>
                        <p class="text-xs text-content-subtle mt-1">
                            issued &amp; awaiting payment ·
                            <a class="underline underline-offset-2 hover:text-content" href="/finance/aged-receivables">aged receivables</a>
                        </p>
                    }
                </div>
                <div class="rounded-xl border border-line bg-surface px-5 py-4"
                     title="Bank cash after every visible month and the dated flows beyond them — where the selected jobs leave the company if they run to the end as forecast. Undated flows excluded until they earn a date.">
                    <p class="text-[11px] uppercase tracking-wider text-content-subtle font-semibold mb-1">Balance at horizon end</p>
                    @if (!BankReady || !TableReady)
                    {
                        <p class="text-2xl font-semibold text-content flex items-center h-8" role="status" aria-live="polite" aria-busy="true">
                            <JewelIcon Class="w-4 h-4 animate-jewel-pulse" />
                            <span class="sr-only">Loading balance at horizon end</span>
                        </p>
                    }
                    else if (forecastView is not { } view || view.Closing.Length == 0)
                    {
                        <p class="text-sm text-content-muted mt-1">Needs the bank position from Xero.</p>
                    }
                    else
                    {
                        var horizonEnd = view.Closing[^1] + view.LaterNet;
                        <p class="text-2xl font-semibold @(horizonEnd < 0m ? "text-negative" : "text-content")">@Money(horizonEnd)</p>
                        <p class="text-xs text-content-subtle mt-1">after @MonthLabel(view.Axis[^1]) incl. later retention releases</p>
                    }
                </div>
            </div>
        }

        @if (projectsFailed)
        {
            <p class="text-sm text-negative">Couldn't load the project list. The details are in the red bar at the top — reload to try again.</p>
        }
        else
        {
            <div class="mb-3 flex items-center justify-between gap-3 flex-wrap">
                @* The filter is a control, so it is never gated: it renders disabled with a
                   loading label until the project list lands (the loading-states convention). *@
                @if (Projects.Current is null)
                {
                    <select disabled
                            class="rounded-lg border border-line-strong bg-surface-field px-3 py-2 text-sm text-content-subtle">
                        <option>Loading projects…</option>
                    </select>
                }
                else
                {
                    <ProjectMultiSelect Projects="@(Projects.Current!)"
                                        Selected="@selectedIds"
                                        SelectedChanged="OnSelectionChangedAsync" />
                }
                @* Disabled while any selected row failed to load: the on-screen banner discloses
                   the zeros, but a workbook travels without it — retry first, then export. *@
                <ExportToExcelButton FileName="Cash forecast"
                                     Disabled="@(!TableReady || SelectedProjects.Count == 0 || FailedSelectedProjects.Count > 0)"
                                     BuildWorkbook="BuildExportWorkbook" />
            </div>

            @* One gate for everything below: the forecast, the statement and the table are the
               same arithmetic over the same sources, so all of it reveals in one piece. *@
            <LoadGate IsLoading="@(!TableReady)" Prominent="true" Label="Loading project cashflows">
            @if (SelectedProjects.Count == 0)
            {
                <div class="panel p-8 text-center">
                    <p class="text-sm text-content">No projects selected — pick some in the filter above.</p>
                </div>
            }
            else
            {
                @if (FailedSelectedProjects.Count > 0)
                {
                    <p class="rounded-lg bg-negative/10 border border-negative/30 px-3 py-2 text-sm text-negative mb-4">
                        The cash position could not be loaded for @string.Join(", ", FailedSelectedProjects.Select(p => p.Reference)) — those rows show zeros.
                        <button type="button" class="underline underline-offset-2 ml-1" @onclick="RetryFailedAsync">Retry</button>
                    </p>
                }

                var forecast = forecastView!;

                <p class="text-xs text-content-subtle mb-3 max-w-4xl">
                    <span class="font-medium text-content-muted">No signs to decode:</span> the band
                    carries the direction — Cash in adds, Cash out subtracts; only Net movement and
                    the balance are signed. Anything overdue sits in the current month, never the
                    past. Flows with no honest date (no practical-completion date set) sit in
                    Undated and never touch the balance.
                </p>

                @* ── The forecast table: one column per month, rows in two bands, every category
                   expandable to its per-project lines. ── *@
                <div class="rounded-xl border border-line bg-surface overflow-x-auto mb-6">
                    <table class="w-full text-sm border-collapse">
                        <thead class="bg-surface-raised border-b border-line">
                            <tr class="text-left text-[11px] uppercase tracking-wider text-content-subtle font-semibold">
                                <th class="px-4 py-3 min-w-[230px]"></th>
                                @foreach (var month in forecast.Axis)
                                {
                                    <th class="px-3 py-3 text-right whitespace-nowrap">@MonthLabel(month)</th>
                                }
                                <th class="px-3 py-3 text-right whitespace-nowrap border-l border-line"
                                    title="Dated flows beyond the visible months — typically the final retention releases.">Later</th>
                                <th class="px-3 py-3 text-right whitespace-nowrap border-l border-line text-content-subtle"
                                    title="Flows with no honest date — e.g. spreads on a project with no practical-completion date. Kept out of the balance until dated.">Undated</th>
                            </tr>
                        </thead>
                        <tbody>
                            <tr class="border-b border-line">
                                <td colspan="@(forecast.Axis.Length + 3)" class="px-4 pt-4 pb-2 text-[11px] uppercase tracking-wider text-content-subtle font-semibold">Cash in</td>
                            </tr>
                            @foreach (var row in InRows)
                            {
                                @CategoryRow((forecast, row.Category, row.Label, row.Source))
                            }
                            <tr class="border-b border-line">
                                <td colspan="@(forecast.Axis.Length + 3)" class="px-4 pt-4 pb-2 text-[11px] uppercase tracking-wider text-content-subtle font-semibold">Cash out</td>
                            </tr>
                            @foreach (var row in OutRows)
                            {
                                @CategoryRow((forecast, row.Category, row.Label, row.Source))
                            }
                            @* Project movement — the ticked projects' cash in less cash out,
                               before company overheads (FD, 2026-08-17): what the selected jobs
                               themselves move, so the jobs and the overheads read separately. *@
                            <tr class="border-t-2 border-line border-b border-line font-medium">
                                <td class="px-4 py-2.5">
                                    <span class="text-content font-medium">Project movement</span>
                                    <span class="block text-[11px] text-content-faint font-normal">cash in less cash out for the projects ticked — before company overheads</span>
                                </td>
                                @for (var index = 0; index < forecast.Axis.Length; index++)
                                {
                                    var movement = forecast.ProjectNet[index];
                                    <td class="px-3 py-2.5 text-right whitespace-nowrap @(movement < 0m ? "text-negative" : "text-positive")">@Signed(movement)</td>
                                }
                                <td class="px-3 py-2.5 text-right whitespace-nowrap border-l border-line @(forecast.LaterNet < 0m ? "text-negative" : "text-positive")">@Signed(forecast.LaterNet)</td>
                                <td class="px-3 py-2.5 text-right border-l border-line text-content-faint font-normal" title="Undated flows are excluded from the balance until they earn a date.">excluded</td>
                            </tr>
                            @* Company overheads — the interim page-level figure (see the amber
                               notice). The inputs are controls: never gated, editable in place.
                               The default fills every month; a month's own cell can be edited to
                               override just that month (FD, 2026-08-17) — clear it to fall back. *@
                            <tr class="border-b border-line">
                                <td class="px-4 py-2.5">
                                    <span class="text-content font-medium">Company overheads</span>
                                    <span class="block text-[11px] text-content-faint">
                                        default ·
                                        <input type="number" min="0" step="500" value="@overheadsMonthly"
                                               @onchange="OnOverheadsChanged"
                                               class="w-24 rounded border border-line-strong bg-surface-field px-1.5 py-0.5 text-xs text-content" />
                                        £/month — edit a month's cell to change just that month · remembered in this browser, not yet a system setting
                                    </span>
                                </td>
                                @foreach (var month in forecast.Axis)
                                {
                                    var overheadsMonth = month;
                                    var isOverridden = overheadsOverrides.ContainsKey(overheadsMonth);
                                    <td class="px-3 py-2.5 text-right whitespace-nowrap">
                                        <input type="number" min="0" step="500" value="@OverheadsFor(overheadsMonth)"
                                               @onchange="args => OnOverheadMonthChangedAsync(overheadsMonth, args)"
                                               title="@(isOverridden ? "Edited for this month — clear it to return to the default" : "The default — edit to override this month only")"
                                               class="w-20 rounded border bg-surface-field px-1.5 py-0.5 text-xs text-content text-right @(isOverridden ? "border-accent" : "border-line-strong")" />
                                    </td>
                                }
                                <td class="px-3 py-2.5 text-right border-l border-line text-content-faint">—</td>
                                <td class="px-3 py-2.5 text-right border-l border-line text-content-faint">—</td>
                            </tr>
                            @* ── The running answer ── *@
                            <tr class="border-t-2 border-line border-b border-line font-semibold">
                                <td class="px-4 py-3 text-content">
                                    Net movement
                                    <span class="block text-[11px] text-content-faint font-normal">project movement less company overheads</span>
                                </td>
                                @for (var index = 0; index < forecast.Axis.Length; index++)
                                {
                                    var net = forecast.Net[index];
                                    <td class="px-3 py-3 text-right whitespace-nowrap @(net < 0m ? "text-negative" : "text-positive")">@Signed(net)</td>
                                }
                                <td class="px-3 py-3 text-right whitespace-nowrap border-l border-line @(forecast.LaterNet < 0m ? "text-negative" : "text-positive")">@Signed(forecast.LaterNet)</td>
                                <td class="px-3 py-3 text-right border-l border-line text-content-faint font-normal" title="Undated flows are excluded from the balance until they earn a date.">excluded</td>
                            </tr>
                            @if (IsDirector && forecast.Closing.Length > 0)
                            {
                                <tr class="bg-surface-raised font-semibold">
                                    <td class="px-4 py-3 text-content">
                                        Closing bank balance
                                        <span class="block text-[11px] text-content-faint font-normal">directors only · seeded from Xero</span>
                                    </td>
                                    @for (var index = 0; index < forecast.Axis.Length; index++)
                                    {
                                        var balance = forecast.Closing[index];
                                        <td class="px-3 py-3 text-right whitespace-nowrap @(balance < 0m ? "text-negative" : "text-content") @(index == forecast.MinIndex ? "ring-2 ring-inset ring-negative rounded" : "")"
                                            title="@(index == forecast.MinIndex ? "The low point — the month to plan for" : null)">@Money(balance)</td>
                                    }
                                    <td class="px-3 py-3 text-right whitespace-nowrap border-l border-line">@Money(forecast.Closing[^1] + forecast.LaterNet)</td>
                                    <td class="px-3 py-3 text-right border-l border-line text-content-faint font-normal">—</td>
                                </tr>
                            }
                        </tbody>
                    </table>
                </div>

                @* ── The balance drawn: one line, the trough flagged. Directors only — it is the
                   bank position over time. ── *@
                @if (IsDirector && forecast.Closing.Length > 1)
                {
                    <div class="rounded-xl border border-line bg-surface px-5 py-4 mb-6">
                        <p class="text-[11px] uppercase tracking-wider text-content-subtle font-semibold mb-2">Closing bank balance by month</p>
                        <ForecastBalanceChart Axis="forecast.Axis" Closing="forecast.Closing"
                                              MinIndex="forecast.MinIndex"
                                              HighReference="@(BankSnapshot?.TotalCash ?? 0m)" />
                    </div>
                }

                @* ── The promise, checked live: phased months per project must equal that
                   project's completion cashflow on the statement below — to the penny. ── *@
                @if (forecast.Variances.Count == 0)
                {
                    <p class="text-xs text-content-subtle mb-10 max-w-4xl">
                        <span class="text-positive font-semibold">✓ Ties to the statement below, to the penny.</span>
                        Every project's phased months (dated, later and undated together) sum to its
                        Project Completion Cashflow — the forecast is the same figures spread in
                        time, never a second opinion.
                    </p>
                }
                else
                {
                    <p class="rounded-lg bg-negative/10 border border-negative/30 px-3 py-2 text-xs text-negative mb-10 max-w-4xl">
                        Phasing does not explain the statement for
                        @string.Join(", ", forecast.Variances.Select(variance => $"{variance.Project.Reference} ({Signed(variance.Variance)})"))
                        — this is a defect to report, not a judgement call. The statement below remains authoritative.
                    </p>
                }

                @* ════════════════════════ the divider ════════════════════════ *@
                <div class="flex items-center gap-4 mb-6">
                    <div class="h-px bg-line flex-1"></div>
                    <p class="text-[11px] uppercase tracking-wider text-content-subtle font-semibold whitespace-nowrap">Position to completion — the former Cash Summary</p>
                    <div class="h-px bg-line flex-1"></div>
                </div>
                <p class="text-xs text-content-subtle mb-4 max-w-4xl">
                    The to-completion statement this page grew out of, unchanged: no time axis, just
                    where the selected jobs' cash lands if they run to the end. The forecast above is
                    these same figures with "when" added. The old bank tiles are not repeated here —
                    their figures live in the strip at the top.
                </p>

                @* ── The combined statement: the selected projects' Cashflow tabs summed into one
                   whiteboard — the same rows, the same helpers, over the table's own figures, so
                   the statement and the rows beneath it agree to the penny. With one project
                   ticked this IS that project's statement. ── *@
                var combined = Totals();
                <div class="rounded-xl border border-line bg-surface mb-8 max-w-2xl">
                    <div class="px-4 py-3 border-b-2 border-line">
                        <p class="text-[11px] uppercase tracking-wider text-content-subtle font-semibold">Combined statement</p>
                        <p class="text-sm font-semibold text-content mt-0.5">@SelectionLabel</p>
                    </div>

                    <div class="flex items-baseline justify-between gap-4 px-4 py-3">
                        <div>
                            <p class="text-sm font-semibold text-content"
                               title="The valuation reports' counting lines — contract works, provisional sums, contingency and variations — summed across the selected projects">Project claim</p>
                            <p class="text-xs text-content-subtle mt-0.5">The full value of the works as currently valued</p>
                        </div>
                        <p class="text-lg font-semibold text-content whitespace-nowrap">@Money(combined.ProjectClaim)</p>
                    </div>

                    <div class="flex items-baseline justify-between gap-4 px-4 py-3 border-t border-line">
                        <div>
                            <p class="text-sm font-semibold text-content"
                               title="Valuation invoices clients have paid, plus retention withheld on works complete (held less confirmed releases, from each project's retention terms)">Cash allocated</p>
                            <p class="text-xs text-content-subtle mt-0.5">
                                @Money(combined.CashReceived) received from clients · @Money(combined.RetentionOutstanding) held in retention
                            </p>
                        </div>
                        <p class="text-lg font-semibold text-content whitespace-nowrap">@Money(-combined.CashAllocated)</p>
                    </div>

                    <div class="flex items-baseline justify-between gap-4 px-4 py-3 border-t-2 border-line">
                        <div>
                            <p class="text-sm font-semibold text-content"
                               title="Project claim less cash allocated, less the retention that will be withheld on the works still to value — what can actually be invoiced to clients before the releases">Left to claim</p>
                            @if (combined.RetentionStillToWithhold != 0m)
                            {
                                <p class="text-xs text-content-subtle mt-0.5"
                                   title="Valuation invoices are raised net of retention, so this slice of the remainder is never invoiceable on a valuation — it comes back through the release rows below instead">
                                    less @Money(combined.RetentionStillToWithhold) retention to be withheld on works left to value
                                </p>
                            }
                            @if (combined.InvoicedAwaitingPayment != 0m)
                            {
                                <p class="text-xs text-content-subtle mt-0.5">of which @Money(combined.InvoicedAwaitingPayment) already invoiced &amp; awaiting payment</p>
                            }
                        </div>
                        <p class="text-lg font-semibold text-content whitespace-nowrap">@Money(combined.LeftToClaim)</p>
                    </div>

                    <div class="flex items-baseline justify-between gap-4 px-4 py-3 border-t border-line">
                        <div>
                            <p class="text-sm text-content"
                               title="Each Financials tab's drawdown to the penny — every cost centre's unspent target cost, with finalised lines realised to profit / loss and reconciliation packages accounted for. Overspent centres are not netted off: the forecast spends the full drawdown and never assumes an overspend is bought back.">Cost centre drawdowns</p>
                            <p class="text-xs text-content-subtle mt-0.5">Budget still expected to be spent, on top of orders and bills</p>
                        </div>
                        <p class="text-base font-semibold text-content whitespace-nowrap">@Money(-combined.Drawdown)</p>
                    </div>

                    <div class="flex items-baseline justify-between gap-4 px-4 py-3 border-t border-line">
                        <div>
                            <p class="text-sm text-content"
                               title="Work-order value not yet invoiced by suppliers — committed spend still to bill; see each project's WO Allocation tab">Uninvoiced work orders</p>
                            <p class="text-xs text-content-subtle mt-0.5">@Money(combined.WoCommitted) committed · @Money(combined.WoInvoiced) invoiced to date</p>
                        </div>
                        <p class="text-base font-semibold text-content whitespace-nowrap">@Money(-combined.WoLeftToInvoice)</p>
                    </div>

                    <div class="flex items-baseline justify-between gap-4 px-4 py-3 border-t border-line">
                        <div>
                            <p class="text-sm text-content"
                               title="The net still owed on allocated purchase lines, part-payment aware: a bill Xero has partly settled counts only its remainder, from the bill's AmountDue as last synced">Unpaid Xero purchase invoices</p>
                        </div>
                        <p class="text-base font-semibold @(combined.BillsUnpaid == 0m ? "text-content" : "text-negative") whitespace-nowrap">@Money(-combined.BillsUnpaid)</p>
                    </div>

                    <div class="flex items-baseline justify-between gap-4 px-4 py-3 border-t border-line">
                        <div>
                            <p class="text-sm text-content"
                               title="The first retention releases still forecast, due at each project's practical completion. A confirmed release has moved into the claim, so it is no longer added back here.">Retention release 1</p>
                            <p class="text-xs text-content-subtle mt-0.5">Still forecast, due at practical completion</p>
                        </div>
                        <p class="text-base font-semibold text-content whitespace-nowrap">@AddBack(combined.Release1)</p>
                    </div>

                    <div class="flex items-baseline justify-between gap-4 px-4 py-3 border-t-2 border-line">
                        <p class="text-sm font-semibold text-content"
                           title="Left to claim, less cost centre drawdowns, uninvoiced work orders and unpaid purchase invoices, plus the first retention releases — the net cash movement between now and practical completion">Practical completion cashflow</p>
                        <p class="text-xl font-semibold @(combined.PracticalCompletionCashflow < 0m ? "text-negative" : "text-positive") whitespace-nowrap">@Money(combined.PracticalCompletionCashflow)</p>
                    </div>

                    <div class="flex items-baseline justify-between gap-4 px-4 py-3 border-t border-line">
                        <div>
                            <p class="text-sm text-content"
                               title="The final retention releases still forecast, due after each project's defects period. A confirmed release has moved into the claim, so it is no longer added back here.">Retention release 2</p>
                            <p class="text-xs text-content-subtle mt-0.5">Still forecast, due after the defects period</p>
                        </div>
                        <p class="text-base font-semibold text-content whitespace-nowrap">@AddBack(combined.Release2)</p>
                    </div>

                    <div class="flex items-baseline justify-between gap-4 px-4 py-3 border-t-2 border-line">
                        <p class="text-sm font-semibold text-content"
                           title="Practical completion cashflow plus the final retention releases — the selected projects' net cash movement to the end of their defects periods">Project completion cashflow</p>
                        <p class="text-xl font-semibold @(combined.ProjectCompletionCashflow < 0m ? "text-negative" : "text-positive") whitespace-nowrap">@Money(combined.ProjectCompletionCashflow)</p>
                    </div>
                </div>

                <div class="rounded-xl border border-line bg-surface overflow-x-auto">
                    <table class="w-full text-sm border-collapse">
                        <thead class="bg-surface-raised border-b border-line">
                            <tr class="text-left text-[11px] uppercase tracking-wider text-content-subtle font-semibold">
                                <th class="px-4 py-3 min-w-[220px]">Project</th>
                                <th class="px-4 py-3 text-right whitespace-nowrap" title="The valuation report's counting lines — the full value of the works as currently valued.">Project Claim</th>
                                <th class="px-4 py-3 text-right whitespace-nowrap" title="Valuation invoices the client has paid, plus retention withheld on works complete.">Cash Allocated</th>
                                <th class="px-4 py-3 text-right whitespace-nowrap border-l border-line" title="Project claim less cash allocated, less the retention that will be withheld on the works still to value — what can actually be invoiced before the releases.">Left to Claim</th>
                                <th class="px-4 py-3 text-right whitespace-nowrap" title="The Financials tab's drawdown to the penny — budget still expected to be spent, on top of orders and bills. Drawdown side only: overspent centres are not netted off.">Drawdowns</th>
                                <th class="px-4 py-3 text-right whitespace-nowrap" title="Work-order value not yet invoiced by suppliers — committed spend still to bill.">Uninvoiced WOs</th>
                                <th class="px-4 py-3 text-right whitespace-nowrap" title="The net still owed on allocated purchase lines, part-payment aware: a part-paid bill counts only its remainder.">Unpaid Bills</th>
                                <th class="px-4 py-3 text-right whitespace-nowrap" title="The first retention release where still forecast — due at practical completion. A confirmed release has moved into the claim.">Retention R1</th>
                                <th class="px-4 py-3 text-right whitespace-nowrap border-l border-line" title="Left to claim, less drawdowns, uninvoiced work orders and unpaid bills, plus the first retention release — the net cash movement to practical completion.">PC Cashflow</th>
                                <th class="px-4 py-3 text-right whitespace-nowrap" title="The final retention release where still forecast — due after the defects period.">Retention R2</th>
                                <th class="px-4 py-3 text-right whitespace-nowrap" title="Practical completion cashflow plus the final retention release — the project's net cash movement to the end of the defects period.">Completion Cashflow</th>
                            </tr>
                        </thead>
                        <tbody class="divide-y divide-line">
                            @foreach (var project in SelectedProjects)
                            {
                                var row = RowFor(project.ProjectId);
                                <tr>
                                    <td class="px-4 py-3 whitespace-nowrap">
                                        <a href="@($"/projects/{project.ProjectId}/cashflow")" class="hover:underline underline-offset-4">
                                            <span class="font-mono text-[11px] text-content-subtle mr-2">@project.Reference</span>
                                            <span class="text-content font-medium">@project.Name</span>
                                        </a>
                                    </td>
                                    <td class="px-4 py-3 text-right whitespace-nowrap text-content">@Money(row.ProjectClaim)</td>
                                    <td class="px-4 py-3 text-right whitespace-nowrap text-content">@Money(-row.CashAllocated)</td>
                                    <td class="px-4 py-3 text-right whitespace-nowrap text-content border-l border-line">@Money(row.LeftToClaim)</td>
                                    <td class="px-4 py-3 text-right whitespace-nowrap text-content">@Money(-row.Drawdown)</td>
                                    <td class="px-4 py-3 text-right whitespace-nowrap text-content">@Money(-row.WoLeftToInvoice)</td>
                                    <td class="px-4 py-3 text-right whitespace-nowrap @(row.BillsUnpaid == 0m ? "text-content" : "text-negative")">@Money(-row.BillsUnpaid)</td>
                                    <td class="px-4 py-3 text-right whitespace-nowrap text-content-muted">@AddBack(row.Release1)</td>
                                    <td class="px-4 py-3 text-right whitespace-nowrap font-medium border-l border-line @(row.PracticalCompletionCashflow < 0m ? "text-negative" : "text-positive")">@Money(row.PracticalCompletionCashflow)</td>
                                    <td class="px-4 py-3 text-right whitespace-nowrap text-content-muted">@AddBack(row.Release2)</td>
                                    <td class="px-4 py-3 text-right whitespace-nowrap font-medium @(row.ProjectCompletionCashflow < 0m ? "text-negative" : "text-positive")">@Money(row.ProjectCompletionCashflow)</td>
                                </tr>
                            }
                        </tbody>
                        @if (SelectedProjects.Count > 1)
                        {
                            var total = Totals();
                            <tfoot class="border-t border-line bg-surface-raised">
                                <tr class="font-semibold">
                                    <td class="px-4 py-3 text-content">All projects</td>
                                    <td class="px-4 py-3 text-right whitespace-nowrap text-content">@Money(total.ProjectClaim)</td>
                                    <td class="px-4 py-3 text-right whitespace-nowrap text-content">@Money(-total.CashAllocated)</td>
                                    <td class="px-4 py-3 text-right whitespace-nowrap text-content border-l border-line">@Money(total.LeftToClaim)</td>
                                    <td class="px-4 py-3 text-right whitespace-nowrap text-content">@Money(-total.Drawdown)</td>
                                    <td class="px-4 py-3 text-right whitespace-nowrap text-content">@Money(-total.WoLeftToInvoice)</td>
                                    <td class="px-4 py-3 text-right whitespace-nowrap @(total.BillsUnpaid == 0m ? "text-content" : "text-negative")">@Money(-total.BillsUnpaid)</td>
                                    <td class="px-4 py-3 text-right whitespace-nowrap text-content-muted">@AddBack(total.Release1)</td>
                                    <td class="px-4 py-3 text-right whitespace-nowrap border-l border-line @(total.PracticalCompletionCashflow < 0m ? "text-negative" : "text-positive")">@Money(total.PracticalCompletionCashflow)</td>
                                    <td class="px-4 py-3 text-right whitespace-nowrap text-content-muted">@AddBack(total.Release2)</td>
                                    <td class="px-4 py-3 text-right whitespace-nowrap @(total.ProjectCompletionCashflow < 0m ? "text-negative" : "text-positive")">@Money(total.ProjectCompletionCashflow)</td>
                                </tr>
                            </tfoot>
                        }
                    </table>
                </div>
                <p class="text-xs text-content-subtle mt-3 max-w-3xl">
                    Each row is that project's Cashflow tab collapsed to a line — the same sources,
                    the same arithmetic, to the penny. Cash allocated counts valuation invoices the
                    client has paid plus retention withheld on works complete; left to claim is net
                    of the retention still to be withheld on works left to value; drawdowns reuse
                    the Financials tab's drawdown-only figure (overspends are not netted off, so
                    the forecast never assumes they are bought back); unpaid bills are
                    part-payment aware; a
                    retention release is only added back while it is still forecast. Click a
                    project for the full statement.
                </p>
            }
            </LoadGate>
        }
    </section>
</ApprovedSessionGate>


@code {
    // One rendering for a forecast category row plus its per-project lines, shared by both
    // bands so cash in and cash out can never drift apart in shape (a templated delegate,
    // like SideNav's ProjectOption).
    private RenderFragment<(ForecastView Forecast, ForecastCategory Category, string Label, string Source)> CategoryRow => context =>
        @<text>
        @{
            var forecast = context.Forecast;
            var category = context.Category;
            var label = context.Label;
            var source = context.Source;
            var expanded = expandedCategories.Contains(category);
            var contributors = forecast.PerProject[category];
        }
        <tr class="border-b border-line">
            <td class="px-4 py-2.5">
                <button type="button" class="text-left" @onclick="() => ToggleCategory(category)"
                        title="@(expanded ? "Collapse the per-project lines" : "Expand to one line per project")">
                    <span class="inline-block w-3 text-content-subtle transition-transform @(expanded ? "rotate-90" : "")">▸</span>
                    <span class="text-content font-medium hover:text-accent">@label</span>
                </button>
                <span class="block pl-3 text-[11px] text-content-faint">@source</span>
            </td>
            @for (var index = 0; index < forecast.Axis.Length; index++)
            {
                <td class="px-3 py-2.5 text-right whitespace-nowrap text-content">@CellAmount(forecast.Cells[category][index])</td>
            }
            <td class="px-3 py-2.5 text-right whitespace-nowrap border-l border-line text-content-muted">@CellAmount(forecast.Later[category])</td>
            <td class="px-3 py-2.5 text-right whitespace-nowrap border-l border-line text-content-subtle">@CellAmount(forecast.Undated[category])</td>
        </tr>
        @if (expanded)
        {
            @if (contributors.Count == 0)
            {
                <tr class="border-b border-line">
                    <td colspan="@(forecast.Axis.Length + 3)" class="px-4 pl-7 py-2 text-xs text-content-subtle italic">Nothing forecast in this category for the selected projects.</td>
                </tr>
            }
            @foreach (var (project, phased) in contributors)
            {
                <tr class="border-b border-line">
                    <td class="px-4 pl-7 py-2 whitespace-nowrap">
                        <a href="@($"/projects/{project.ProjectId}/cashflow")" class="text-xs text-content-muted hover:text-content hover:underline underline-offset-4"
                           title="This project's full statement — the figures this line is spread from">
                            <span class="font-mono text-[10px] text-content-subtle mr-1.5">@project.Reference</span>@project.Name
                        </a>
                        @if (category == ForecastCategory.FutureValuations)
                        {
                            @* The FD's two knobs (2026-08-13), inline like the overheads input —
                               controls, so never gated. Stored on the project via their own
                               commands; the API gate (Director/FD/PM) is the authority, and a
                               refusal lands on the error toast like any failed command. *@
                            <span class="block mt-1 text-[10px] text-content-faint whitespace-nowrap">
                                next valuation
                                <input type="date" value="@(project.NextExpectedValuationDate?.ToString("yyyy-MM-dd"))"
                                       @onchange="args => OnNextValuationChangedAsync(project, args)"
                                       title="The full date matters: each valuation is paid the contract's payment terms after this day of the month, so cash lands on payment dates"
                                       class="rounded border border-line-strong bg-surface-field px-1 py-0.5 text-[10px] text-content mx-1" />
                                · expects
                                <input type="number" min="0" step="1000" placeholder="even"
                                       value="@(project.ExpectedMonthlyValuation?.ToString("0"))"
                                       @onchange="args => OnMonthlyValuationChangedAsync(project, args)"
                                       class="w-20 rounded border border-line-strong bg-surface-field px-1 py-0.5 text-[10px] text-content mx-1" />
                                £/month · blank = spread evenly to practical completion
                            </span>
                        }
                    </td>
                    @for (var index = 0; index < forecast.Axis.Length; index++)
                    {
                        <td class="px-3 py-2 text-right whitespace-nowrap text-xs text-content-muted">@CellAmount(phased.Months[index])</td>
                    }
                    <td class="px-3 py-2 text-right whitespace-nowrap border-l border-line text-xs text-content-muted">@CellAmount(phased.Later)</td>
                    <td class="px-3 py-2 text-right whitespace-nowrap border-l border-line text-xs text-content-subtle">@CellAmount(phased.Undated)</td>
                </tr>
            }
        }
        </text>;
}
